{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>And the dove came to him at evening time, etc.</b> What does it matter to us whether she came in the evening and returned in the morning or the reverse? And according to what appears, that she brought him an olive leaf in order to produce from them light — for it was precisely at evening time that they needed it. For according to the one who says that ״צֹהַר״ means a window, it is difficult: at night, what would illuminate for him? Therefore the Hizkuni explained ״צֹהַר״ in the sense of יִצְהָר — olive oil — that he would kindle oil in the ark at night, and by day the light entered through the window of the ark, as it is written: ״וַיִּפְתַּח נֹחַ אֶת חַלּוֹן הַתֵּבָה אֲשֶׁר עָשָׂה״ (Genesis 8:6). And a proof for these matters is what is brought in Midrash Tanchuma (5) and in the Yalkut, parashat Tetzaveh, on the verse ״עֵינַיִךְ יוֹנִים״ (Song of Songs 4:1): 'Just as the dove brought light to the world, so you — bring olive oil and kindle lamps before Him,' etc. And it is difficult: from where does the author of this midrash know that the dove brought light to the world, and how did he learn this from the verse ״וְהִנֵּה עֲלֵה זַיִת טָרָף בְּפִיהָ״? Rather, it is certain that he learned this from what is stated ״לְעֵת עֶרֶב״, as stated." "And as for what Rashi explained — 'the dove said: let my sustenance be bitter as the olive,' etc. — the meaning is not that she literally said so with her mouth, for the dove is not a creature of speech from yesterday or the day before. Rather, we understand from the fact that she brought for her food an olive leaf — a very bitter food. And did the dove not know that she has a constant meal upon the table of Noah, day by day? Rather, it is certain that she chose this bitter food because it was in the hands of Heaven and not in the hands of flesh and blood."], :book :genesis, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:27:39.542526323Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}